From 6578a7394df0da6d2da1f91de438e69a4aa74183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:59:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Run FormCalc scripts

FormCalc is the default script language of XFA, used by scripts without
a contentType, and these ran as JavaScript, failing. Forms use it for
calculations such as Sum(Row[*].Amount) and date checks.

FormCalc scripts are now translated to JavaScript by a recursive
descent parser, and run on a runtime that keeps FormCalc's semantics:
references resolve when used, null counts as 0 in arithmetic, operators
give 1 or 0, and the value of a script is that of its last expression.
The translator covers the whole language but predicates in SOM
expressions, and the runtime the arithmetic, string and date functions.

Functions of script objects now run with the script object as this,
falling back to its owner, so that they can call each other through
this as forms expect.

Across the corpus, script errors in dynamic forms go from 112 to 21.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
